.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
.TH OCTA-PROBE 1 "" "OCTA-CAPTURE @PROJECT_VERSION@" "OCTA-CAPTURE Manual"
.SH NAME
octa\-probe \- read a raw USB clock diagnostic
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBocta-probe\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Find an accessible OCTA-CAPTURE base or EXP USB device with libusb and read clock status.
Print the actual device VID:PID, sample_rate_hz and raw clock_flags as JSON.
This developer diagnostic uses raw USB access; normal installed clients should
prefer octa-status(1), which reads through the kernel driver.
Device detection and a successful clock query do not prove audio streaming.

.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success; nonzero indicates a usage, device or operation error.
.SH SEE ALSO
octa-capture(1), octa-status(1), octa-preset(1)
